A||N||10||David Bartlett||Whining Noise?||||1||
Z||000000||David Bartlett||09-29-2001||01:55 AM||||Last night while driving home I notice a strange whining noise (like and electric motor) coming from directly behind the fire wall. It sounded like it was in the centre of the car but I cant be for certain. I can only hear it when the cars at idel.  It seems to fluctuate with the engine rpms (another problem Ive been having, only about 100  rpm fluctuation).<P>Is it the altinator, waterpump, fuelpump?<P>What would be the expect life of these device from the state its in?||||reg||1
Z||000001||kempo||09-29-2001||10:43 AM||||If you have installed an amplifier with your stereo system, the whining noise may be coming from your speakers due to a bad ground.  This should happen only while the engine is on, and will whine with the rpms (ie- if you step on the accelerator to rev your engine, the noise will get high/louder in tune).  If you engine is off, your radio should play normally.  If it is not your radio at all, my 2 cents would be to check the alternator.  I hope this helps.  Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/kempsig.jpg"> <BR>87 Fiero GT / 5 Speed<BR>86 Fiero 2m4 - FOR SALE||||reg||1
Z||000002||David Bartlett||09-29-2001||11:34 AM||||I'm 100% sure its no the stereo.. Is it a difficult job to remove the altinator and have it tested? I realize that it requires removing the electrical connections, unbolting the bracket but what I'm concerned with is the belts... is that difficult?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fldevel||09-29-2001||12:20 PM||||sounds like the fuel pump ..after all the fuel tank is right between the seats i can hear the fuel pump whine in pretty much all my fieros if i listen carefully ..it is usualy a bit louder when hte gas tank is closer to empty ||||reg||1
Z||000004||David Bartlett||09-29-2001||12:34 PM||||I just filled her up yesturday, so I wouldn't be low on gas. My dad has a noisy fuel pump in his car, maybe ill take a listen to that and compair the sound.  Im still leaning towards the altinator though...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever3000||09-29-2001||01:03 PM||||My alternator is doing that.  It even stopped working one day, then started working again the next.  It's gonna stop again soon, but I can't afford to replace it now, so I'm just driving with my fingers crossed.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||09-29-2001||01:46 PM||||My alternator has been noisy since I got the car in April. Almost sounds like a turbine.<BR>Today when I started it up, it almost sounded like it was growling. Volt gauge swung about halfway down the negative scale when I turned on the AC. When I stopped for gas, I left the engine running and wiggled the connector on the edge of the alternator. The growl changed noticeably. After a few minutes, it started charging normally and the growl was gone. <BR>Waiting for it wave buh-bye, though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||SLYGUY||09-29-2001||01:57 PM||||When I first looked at my car at the little dealership I bought it from a couple of months ago the engine ran well. No rough idle, no whirs, squeaks, or whines. <P>On the way home, it started a whine that I had heard before on a different car. On the previous car (84 GTI) it turned out to be the water pump. I wasn't paying close enough attention to the charge gauge, but all of my electrical was running solely off of the battery. The alternator was whining loudly, and NOT running the car's electrical or charging the battery.<P>Turned out to be an easy fix though. Put the left rear of the car up on a ramp. I put a jack and jackstand on the right rear. Removed the wheel and everything was within easy reach. Loosened up the alternator to swing it loose from the bolt, removed the top bolt and bracket. Unplugged the bad alternator and it fell out. <P>Went to NAPA and they had an exact replacement for $109. Easy fix start to finish.<P>Sly<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||09-29-2001||02:51 PM||||Sly,<P>Is yours an automatic or a 5-speed?<BR>I've heard the automatics are a real b!tch when you need to change the alternator. Pre-88s, anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||David Bartlett||09-29-2001||03:47 PM||||Neither, 4spd 2.8.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jncomutt||09-29-2001||04:27 PM||||THANK YOU KEMPO!!!!<P>I have the whining noise from my left speakers only when I have both my amps hooked up.  (1 for the 2 10" subs and 1 for the speakers.)  If I have only one amp its fine, but when both are hooked up I get the whine.  I can't wait to go play with the ground wire, hope it works!!!||||reg||1
